Z||000000||making it better||03-21-2000||12:00 AM||||Problem 1 - when i start my car(87 fiero gt) it will only start if i push the accelerator.  I have cleaned the injectors and also gave it a tune up, but it hasn't fixed the problem.  it runs fine other than that.<P>problem 2 - when i drive about 110km/hour my engine light comes on.  when i read the computer it comes up as the EGR system code.  i check the egr valve and it wasn't working great so i replaced it, but the light still comes on.<P>I would appreciate any suggestions.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||03-21-2000||02:12 AM||||Problem one and two are related. You have a vacuum leak or your cat converter is going bad. For vacuum leaks it's either the tube that goes from EGR to intake (V-6) has a crack in it or the ERG vacuum/soliniod switch is bad/broken.||||reg||1
Z||000002||making it better||03-21-2000||07:52 PM||||thanks.<P>I am glad i found this site it is great.  I don't have to look at the car for hours and try to figure the problem out.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||03-21-2000||09:08 PM||||making it better,<P>I bet you that you got a code 32, right?<P>If so, it means one of two things ...<P>One, like posted earlier, a vacuum leak on one of the little black tubes running from the EGR valve and the EGR solenoid.<P>Two, the EGR solenoid isn't working properly (or at all) and it isn't signaling the ECM that it is controling the EGR valve.<P>I have had the EGR Solenoid go bad on me and got the same indications.  Only sets the code @ sustained higher speeds (i.e. 65+mph)<P>Paul<BR><p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 03-21-2000).]||||reg||4
